WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.201
FedRAMP success depends on collaboration among many stakeholders.

2
00:00:04.201 --> 00:00:15.216
Cloud providers, federal agencies, engineers, administrators, security teams, compliance personnel, assessors, and leadership all contribute to the program.

3
00:00:15.216 --> 00:00:27.409
Cloud service providers are responsible for building and operating cloud offerings, implementing controls, maintaining documentation, responding to findings, and supporting ongoing monitoring activities.

4
00:00:27.409 --> 00:00:39.262
Federal agencies are responsible for understanding their mission needs, reviewing available security information, making risk decisions for their own use cases, and monitoring the services they rely on.

5
00:00:39.262 --> 00:00:43.782
Assessors evaluate control implementation and provide assessment results.

6
00:00:43.782 --> 00:00:52.812
Security and compliance teams coordinate documentation, evidence, findings, risk discussions, and communication across stakeholders.

7
00:00:52.812 --> 00:01:07.070
Engineers and administrators make FedRAMP real through architecture, identity management, logging, encryption, vulnerability management, change control, automation, incident response, and operational support.

8
00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:12.707
Leadership matters because authorization and risk management require accountable decisions.

9
00:01:12.707 --> 00:01:19.671
Leaders provide priorities, resources, expectations, and support for remediation and continuous improvement.

10
00:01:19.671 --> 00:01:25.977
The shared responsibility model is important because cloud security is not owned by one group alone.

11
00:01:25.977 --> 00:01:32.642
FedRAMP works best when each stakeholder understands what they own and how their work affects the security posture.

12
00:01:32.642 --> 00:01:34.898
Clear roles also reduce friction.

13
00:01:34.898 --> 00:01:46.093
When teams know who owns documentation, who fixes findings, who approves changes, and who communicates with assessors or agencies, the program becomes easier to operate.
